Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Permanently tells Microsoft Edge on THIS device to treat the address
; below as a secure origin, so the microphone (voice recording) works
; no matter how the page is opened — typed address, shortcut, or the
; kiosk launcher script.
;
; NOT needed if the kiosk browser and the server run on the SAME
; machine and the kiosk .bat points at http://localhost:3000 — Edge
; already treats localhost as secure natively, no policy required.
; Only apply this .reg (and edit the IP below to match) when a kiosk
; touchscreen is a SEPARATE physical device reaching the server over
; the LAN by IP, e.g. http://192.168.x.x:3000 — replace the address
; below with that real value first.
;
; Run this file, click through the "Add to registry?" prompt
; (admin rights required), then FULLY close every Edge window
; before reopening — the policy is only read at browser startup.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge\OverrideSecurityRestrictionsOnInsecureOrigin]
"1"="http://REPLACE-WITH-SERVER-LAN-IP:3000"
